  "narrative": {
    "intro": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligated $13.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. TriWest received 23 awards, with an average award size of $596M, and obligations are up 2.5% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for the largest share of federal buying with $9B in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $4.7B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the dominant market for TriWest, with $13.5B in obligations. Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds is a distant second market with $261M in obligations. Historical obligations show steady growth from FY21 through FY26, moving from $6.7B in FY21 to $13.7B in FY26. The current-year totals are partial because FY2026 to date is a fiscal year to date snapshot, and the largest-agency and market totals reflect where most federal obligations are concentrated. That concentration helps explain why a small number of large awards account for a high average award size.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are TriWest Healthcare Alliance’s federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $9B to TriWest Healthcare Alliance, and the Department of Defense obligated $4.7B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers accounted for $13.5B in obligations, making that NAICS dominant. The two named markets together include the large majority of obligations, while the next market recorded $261M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $6.7B in FY21 to $13.7B in FY26. Obligations increased every reported year, with $7.4B in FY22, $8B in FY23, $8.4B in FY24, and $13.4B in FY25. The FY2026 to date figure of $13.7B reflects partial-year totals and shows obligations up 2.5% year over year."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does TriWest Healthcare Alliance make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligated $13.7B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. TriWest received 23 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $596M, and obligations are up 2.5% year over year. Historical fiscal-year totals show growth from $6.7B in FY21 through $13.7B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from TriWest Healthcare Alliance?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Defense buy most from TriWest Healthcare Alliance. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $9B and the Department of Defense obligated $4.7B in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does TriWest Healthcare Alliance sell to the government?",
